# 188 · Every agent on Live: each advisor's own lines and chip, what headless advisors do as they work, and Everything

**Status:** `IN_PROGRESS` · **Version:** [v0.1.2](../roadmap.md#v012)

## What

From the owner, 2026-11-03: "Why don't I have a live view of the teachers lines? Like I never know waht the teachers do, waht research they do, etc... Its invisible to me... I only ever see auditor in the advisors lane... can you set teachers lane teacher-1, teacher-2, etc? also same for merger. Essentially I should be able to see all live outputs of all agents ran everywhere".

Every advisor's line went on Live under one source, `supervisor`, so a run's Live had one **Advisors** chip for all of them. An advisor in its program's own terminal sent its text there with its name in front; a headless one, as the merged by model always is, sent only a line for each step of a round, so what a teacher read, searched and ran never showed.

1. **Each advisor's own source.** The supervisor sends an advisor's lines under `advisor:<name>`: `teacher-1`, `teacher-2`, `merged-by`, `auditor`, each reviewer of the review panel, `synthesizer`, `final-writer`. Control takes such unsigned lines from the supervisor, as it takes its own.
2. **A chip for each.** A run's Live has a chip for each advisor that has lines (the merged by model shows as **merger**), beside **Advisors**, which shows them all; each kind of agent has its colour, on its chip and on its lines.
3. **What headless advisors do.** An advisor that runs headless sends its tool calls (what it reads, searches and runs) and its text to Live as it works, where its program reports them as it goes: Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Pi. A `cli` advisor's command shows only its answer.
4. **Everything.** The top of Live's list of runs: every agent's lines from every run and rig as they come, each with its run, with **Rig** and **Run** to narrow it and the same chips.

## Done when

- [ ] The four, with their tests and the pages that describe them (the Live view, how the parts talk), and the steering and control acceptance checks pass.

## Decisions

- 2026-11-03, owner, on the mockup (https://claude.ai/artifact/4cSfguU1uvFXQGmBxNpgTU): "Build it as drawn"; "love the color coding".

## Progress

- 2026-11-03: Goal written from the owner's request, with the mockup the owner approved.
- 2026-11-03: Steps 1 and 2 built (no tests run on the Mac). The live source `advisor:<name>` (core/live.ts, advisorLiveSource), on the subject `…live.advisor-<name>` (core/link/live.ts); control folds an advisor's unsigned lines as the supervisor's (control/live/bus.ts). An advisor's lines in its terminal and in its Pi view go under its source, without its name in front (supervisor/advisors/terminal/). Live tags them with the advisor, its group and `advisors`, names the merged by model merger, and colours each kind of agent (ui/live.ts agentKind, advisorLabel; style/live.ts); a run's Live has a filter for each advisor with lines, which addresses the message box to it (dashboard/live/index.ts). Tests in tests/core/link/live.test.ts, tests/supervisor/live/bus.test.ts and tests/control/ui/live.test.ts. A round's step lines (the teachers review, the portfolio) stay the supervisor's.
- 2026-11-03: Step 4 built (no tests run on the Mac). Everything (dashboard/live/everything.ts) at `/ui/live/everything`, first in Live's list of runs, which moved into dashboard/live/runs.ts for both pages: every rig's newest lines (store/live.ts everywhere, everywhereTail, everywhereCount), each with its run as a link to its Live, narrowed by Rig and Run (a form that applies each choice at once, ui/client.ts), with the filters and colours of a run's Live, and pushed as they come from a feed of every rig (push.ts: a feed without a rig). Test in tests/control/dashboard/live.test.ts. Left: step 3, headless advisors' tool calls and text as they work.
- 2026-11-03: Step 3 built (no tests run on the Mac). A headless advisor's work reaches Live from the supervisor's side: Thermite's tools server for the call tells each tool call it answers (advisors/tools/mcp.ts wraps registerTool), and runAdvisor turns that into a tool line under the advisor's own source when the call names its run and Live's sink (`live`, advisors/run.ts); the teachers, the merged by model, the auditor, each reviewer, the synthesizer and the final writer each pass theirs (advisors/pass/). A call in its own terminal shows its tool calls from its program's transcript instead, and a `cli` command shows only its steps. A program's own built-in tools, where it has any, are not seen this way (a headless Claude Code advisor has none). Test in tests/supervisor/advisors/pass/past.test.ts. All four parts are built; the steering and control acceptance checks are left.
- 2026-11-03: From the owner, after the roll to the lab: "I can see a teacher under the left advisor active, but right advisor is inactive and I see no teacher lines... Line render still sucks btw... I want two toggles. toggle 1 = terminals or lines toggle 2 = which terminal or which line to view." Found on the test rig: teacher-1 (Codex) did not take its message, and teacher-2 (Claude Code) answered in its terminal but its answer was refused. Its answer was written over many lines, and parseAnswer took an object of one line inside it for the answer; its error kept only the answer's last 300 characters. Fixed (no tests run on the Mac): parseAnswer tries each whole object first and names the schema's problems (runtimes/cli.ts answerObjects, noAnswer); each advisor's call has a first and a last line under its own source, so its chip shows from its start and its failure says why (advisors/run.ts); a teacher's review goes under its own source (pass/teachers.ts). The run's Live has the owner's two toggles: Terminals | Lines (`.lseg`), then one row of whose, which in Terminals is the grid's tabs, All first, every lane, the planner and each advisor in its colour, the Advisors tab gone (dashboard/live/index.ts, ui/terminal.ts); the filter `w` holds across both. Tool lines read as what they did (ui/live.ts toolSummary: commands without a shell's wrapper, reads, edits, writes, searches, fetches, MCP names without their server; arguments cut short read field by field), and a rig cuts long arguments string by string so they stay JSON (core/live.ts summarizeArgs). Tests updated: the four the lab's full check found stale, and the terminal, advisor line and tool line tests.
- 2026-11-03: Long messages in a program's own terminal, from the test rig's teachers' rounds. Codex kept a teacher's message (about 100 KB) in its input and Claude Code showed it as seven paste chips: the message went in 16 KB pieces, and a piece with no line break went in as keys, one at a time (the brief is one line of JSON), so each Enter came while the program still typed it. Fixed (no tests run on the Mac; each commit's tests ran on a test machine beside its roll): a message still in the input gets Enter again every 15 s, Claude Code's chips counted, with 30 s more for each 32 KB (agents/cli/terminal.ts); a text of 256 characters or more goes as a paste (agents/terminal/keys.ts). On the test rig the 17:59Z round on the first of these took Claude Code's message and its review; Codex's waits for the paste fix. Released in v0.1.2; the steering and control acceptance checks run in CI on its tag.
- 2026-11-03: On the test rig, the first teachers' round on v0.1.2 (19:00Z) gave both teachers' reviews: Codex took its one-line brief as pastes with no Enter again, and Claude Code its seven pastes. v0.1.2 was released at 21:24Z. CI's first run on a version tag ran the steering and control acceptance checks, with others that had never run; their failures were the checks' own and Docker's (the supervisor had no host.docker.internal), fixed on main after the tag (c9a9ebdb, 89b05921). The next tag's run checks steering and control again; leaf acceptance under Docker is issue 54.

